WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.825
Here's the part nobody sees.

2
00:00:01.825 --> 00:00:05.403
When an instance's service
principal name is missing,

3
00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:10.200
Kerberos quietly gives way to NTLM,
and the application still connects.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.901
The engine doesn't log which protocol
each session used, so an estate that

5
00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:20.150
believes it runs Kerberos can be running
NTLM on a large share of its connections.

6
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.688
Only measurement tells you.

7
00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:26.008
Meanwhile the identities themselves
are anchored in Active Directory,

8
00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:30.401
or in a password the instance checks on
its own, like the built-in sa account.

9
00:00:30.401 --> 00:00:31.975
None of this was a mistake.

10
00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:36.050
It was good engineering for a world
where everything was domain-joined.

11
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.550
That world is ending, and
three drivers are ending it.
